.TH RCMD 1 "2026-09-18" "rcmd 4.34.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rcmd, rcedit, rcview, rcdiff \- an orthodox two-panel file manager with mc's keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rcmd
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIDIR1\fR [\fIDIR2\fR]]
.br
.B rcedit
\fIFILE\fR...
.br
.B rcview
\fIFILE\fR | \fB-\fR
.br
.B rcdiff
\fIFILE1\fR \fIFILE2\fR
.br
.B rcmd --import-mc
[\fIMC_CONFIG_DIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rcmd
is a Midnight Commander replacement: two panels, the command line under
them, a persistent subshell behind Ctrl+O, and mc's key bindings, with a
viewer, an editor, archives, SFTP, FISH and FTP panels, find, compare and
synchronize built in.
.PP
Called as
.BR rcedit ,
.B rcview
or
.B rcdiff
(through a link of that name), it opens the editor, the viewer or the
file comparison on its own, as mc's mcedit, mcview and mcdiff do.
.B rcview -
pages through standard input.
.PP
F1 inside rcmd is the full list of keys, opened at the part about what is
on screen; / searches it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-edit " " \fIFILE\fR
Start in the editor on FILE; repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-view " " \fIFILE\fR
Start in the viewer on FILE; \fB-\fR reads standard input.
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-printwd " " \fIFILE\fR
Write the last active directory to FILE on exit, for a shell wrapper to
cd to (contrib/rc.sh, contrib/rc.fish).
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-skin " " \fINAME\fR
The theme: mc, dark, bw, or a skin of your own.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-nocolor
Black and white.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-color
Colour (the default).
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-colors " " \fISPEC\fR
mc's colour spec: keyword=fg,bg:keyword=fg,bg.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-nomouse
No mouse.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-nosubshell
No persistent subshell.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-subshell
A persistent subshell.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-ftplog " " \fIFILE\fR
Log the FTP and FISH dialogue to FILE.
.TP
.BR \-\-remote " " \fICMD\fR...
Hand the rest of the command line to a running rcmd and exit; put
.B \-\-to
before it.
.TP
.BR \-\-to " " \fIPID\fR
Which running rcmd, when there are several.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print every setting at its default, each line commented out, as a
config.toml to start from.
.TP
.BR \-\-import\-mc " [" \fIDIR\fR ]
Print an rcmd configuration built from mc's user menu, mc.ext and keymap
(default ~/.config/mc, with mc's own files in /etc/mc for anything not
there).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rcmd/config.toml
The configuration: yours, never rewritten by rcmd.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/rcmd/state.toml
What rcmd remembers between sessions: settings changed inside it, the
histories, the hotlist, where each panel and each edited file was.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
HostName, User, Port and IdentityFile for sftp:// and fish:// hosts.
.TP
.I ~/.netrc
Logins and passwords for ftp:// hosts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mc (1),
.BR ssh_config (5),
.BR netrc (5)
